Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 3 08:20:04 2026 +0000

    Panel: cookie-first, official-API-shadow fallback for usage (ADDITIVE, FLAG-OFF)
    
    When the flag is on, the dashboard fills usage from the official-API shadow
    (data/api_shadow/) ONLY for kits that have NO cookie usage — cookie stays primary,
    so "what works with cookie keeps working with cookie; where cookie has nothing, the
    official API provides it," and the customer sees data instead of "no usage yet".
    
    - Two helpers after drLoad(): drOfficialApiUsageRows() (shapes shadow usage.json into
      cookie sl_usage records, joined to kit_number via shadow service_lines.json) and
      drMergeShadowUsage() (appends shadow rows only for kit_numbers absent from cookie).
    - Wired at the three usage pools: the two client-portal builds ($drAllUsage) and the
      fleet-dashboard build ($allUsage -> $usageIdx). One line each.
    - Flag: env DR_OFFICIAL_API_VIEW=yes OR file data/api_shadow/VIEW_ENABLED. Default OFF
      => drMergeShadowUsage returns its input unchanged => byte-identical behaviour.
    - php -l clean; logic smoke-tested (flag off = unchanged; flag on = cookie kits kept,
      gap kits filled from shadow with correct field mapping).
    
    Known limitation: daily_blue/daily_white are empty for shadow rows (the adapter stores
    cycle totals, not daily arrays yet) -> the per-day trend chart is empty for shadow-only
    kits; the hero total + priority/standard split + history total all populate. Daily is a
    small follow-up. Not deployed.
    
